{title: Hymn For The Crossing}
{subtitle:  Amy Speace [2015]}

{define: G base-fret 1 frets 0 0 0 0}
{define: C base-fret 0 frets 0 1 2 0}
{define: Em base-fret 0 frets 0 0 2 0}
{define: D base-fret 0 frets 2 1 0 2}

[G]Don't need a golden [C]box for my [G]bones
Don't need your [Em]weepin' and [C]wai[D]lin'
[C]Dont need my [G]name [Em]carved into [C]stone
Just [G]sing [C]me a [G]hymn [D]for the [C]cross[G]ing
 
[G]Don't speak of nights [C]darkened by [G]regret
Don't speak of [Em]today's light [C]fa[D]ding
[C]Don't speak at all [G]just [Em]sit here by my [C]bed
And [G]sing [C]me a [G]hymn [D]for the [C]cross[G]ing
 
{chorus}
[G]The many [C]miles we have [G]roamed
Each one a [C]mark upon our [D]bones
In the [Em]end we leave [C]alone
So until [G]then, just sing me [D]home
 
[G]Don't fight the tears, the [C]sorrow of the [G]sea
Don't be [Em]afraid when it's [C]ra[D]ging
[C]Don't fight the [G]waves Let them [Em]rock you off to [C]sleep
While you [G]sing [C]me a [G]hymn [D]for the [C]cross[G]ing
 
{chorus}
 
[G]Farewell my friends, [C]although I'd love to [G]stay
Can't keep the [Em]Old Man [C]wai[D]ting
'Cause [C]when he calls for you [G]I'll [Em]be at the [C]gate
To [G]sing [C]you a [G]hymn [D]for the [C]cross[G]ing
To sing [C]you a [G]hymn [D]for the [C]cross[G]ing.
 
